# Intentionally empty.
#
# The old Netlify _redirects file forwarded three things that don't belong
# in this file on Cloudflare:
#
# 1. http -> https on coastalcrawlspaces.net
#    Cloudflare does this automatically. Dashboard -> SSL/TLS -> Edge
#    Certificates -> "Always Use HTTPS" (should already be on by default).
#
# 2. chucktowncrawlspace.com -> coastalcrawlspaces.net
# 3. chucktowncrawl.com -> coastalcrawlspaces.net
#    _redirects only matches requests that already landed on THIS zone
#    (coastalcrawlspaces.net) - it can never catch traffic arriving at a
#    different domain, no matter how it's written. If those old domains
#    are still yours, set the 301 wherever their DNS lives:
#      - If added to this same Cloudflare account as their own zones:
#        Rules -> Redirect Rules (or Bulk Redirects) on each old domain.
#      - If still on GoDaddy: My Products -> DNS -> Forwarding on each
#        old domain, forward to https://coastalcrawlspaces.net, type 301.
